/* =====================================================================
   question-lamp-core.js — the model of ACTIVITY #76 of the one-by-one
   rebuild: "Wren's Question Window" → THE QUESTION LAMP (L.K.1.d, 11
   locales). Design sheet: docs/activities-rebuild/designs/076-wren-question-window.md
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE INVENTION: every question word is a lamp that shines on one KIND of
   answer — who on a person, what on a thing, where on a place, when on a
   time, why on a reason, how on the way. The answer sentence stands under
   a lamp rail as picture cards; one card wears a gold frame. Put a word in
   the question's gap and press Check: the lamp swings to the card of the
   kind that word asks for — onto the gold one when the word is right, onto
   another card (or onto nothing at all) when it is not. Every round has
   exactly ONE right word: the answer strip holds at most one card of each
   kind, and the gold frame decides (the old version had questions with
   two or three right words).
   Levels: who / what / where · + when · + why / how · Match the question to
   its answer (the beam drops into the reply slot) · Sort the answers under
   three lamps. Answer: keys, or Write it (the question word typed).
   WORDS: every question and answer is a literal per-locale string with a
   kind on each chunk (scratchpad ql-content.js); a question word's form
   that depends on the sentence (de wohin, sv vart, es adónde, pt para onde,
   fi mihin / minkä / kenellä …) is authored with its round.
   No DOM. UMD: window.QuestionLampCore / module.exports.
   ===================================================================== */
